# Environment variables — the convention for secrets (see TECH.md → "Dynamism convention").
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development. NEVER commit real secrets — `.env*`
# is gitignored. In production, set these in the Vercel dashboard (Settings → Environment
# Variables). Read them server-side in a route handler via `process.env.<NAME>`.
#
# The foundation does not use any of these yet — they're examples of where a later dynamic
# feature would plug in. Uncomment and fill in as features are added.

# Example: a key for an external API a route handler would call.
# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=

# Example: a Google Sheets webhook / Apps Script URL for logging taps.
# SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL=
